 "notes": "OUTCOME-INFORMED AMENDMENT: after the first two selection decisions (block 0, fixed and grammar, round 1) the selection rule was changed for all arms, blocks and rounds from the registered strict Holm gate to 'most sustained successes among the parent and the candidates within the drop bound, ties to the parent' (advisor consult call_00244; amendment file records both config hashes; no confirmation case had run; the two decisions were recomputed from saved rows; nothing was regenerated or retrained). Under the registered rule all 18 selection decisions would have kept the parent (no candidate reached Holm p < 0.05; smallest 0.106), every finalist would have been the R-106 root and every between-arm contrast exactly 0. Under the amended rule 13 of 18 decisions moved to a candidate. The study is therefore not wholly preregistered. KNOWN SPEC DEFECT, left as registered: the grammar RNG seed is block_seed + 9000 + 10 r + k with consecutive block seeds, so block b's candidate 1 and block b+1's candidate 0 drew the same edit in both rounds; the three blocks are not independent grammar-search replicates and all across-block t intervals (2 degrees of freedom) are nominal and exploratory. The driver was stopped once between simulator children to apply the amendment (my first kill command also killed my own remote shell; the in-flight training child finished and its result was reused; no seeded child was relaunched). RESULT: no arm separates from another or from the R-106 root on fresh cases; all four trained policies sit about +0.12 to +0.13 above the D-072 reference in every block (r106 +0.125 pooled over 4,608 pairs, a second replication of D-075). Fixed continuation (24 more updates) minus the root: +0.009 [-0.006, +0.025] pooled, so the fixed structure's gains have flattened. The pooled case-paired LLM-minus-grammar interval is [-0.006, +0.024] (conditional on these nine finalists), i.e. any advantage of these LLM finalists over these grammar finalists is below +0.05; the registered across-block interval [-0.047, +0.064] contains zero and +0.05. LLM edits: 12 calls, 40,337 tokens, 0 corrections, 0 invalid; in round 1 all three blocks' first proposal was the same term (spin_deficit x tip_dist on groups), reflecting the shared initial information. Selection wins did not predict confirmation: e.g. block 2 fixed led its selections and is the best block-2 finalist (880), block 0 LLM (863) likewise, but block 1's selected fixed and LLM finalists are no better than the root. 2,043,223 starts charged of 2,300,000; 168 confirmation cells (identical policies reused cells)."
